      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "Cancer is a complex, multilevel phenomenon [1-5] in which health outcomes depend on highly interrelated elements across stages of etiology, prevention, screening, diagnosis, treatment, survivorship, and end-of-life care [6, 7]. Standard bench and clinical research approaches alone are not well suited to account for this complexity, as most cancer control interventions often focus on explicit, often linear health outcomes of a specific, well-defined population [1, 8, 9]. To overcome persistent barriers to providing high-quality, equitable care, approaches are needed to address this complexity and provide guidance for successful intervention. ... The extent to which system dynamics modeling has been applied specifically to cancer prevention and control has not been studied.",
      "reason": "Describes current knowledge about cancer complexity and systems science, and identifies the gap in knowledge regarding system dynamics modeling for cancer."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "To overcome persistent barriers to providing high-quality, equitable care, approaches are needed to address this complexity and provide guidance for successful intervention. ... The extent to which system dynamics modeling has been applied specifically to cancer prevention and control has not been studied.",
      "reason": "Explains the need for approaches to address complexity and the lack of study on system dynamics for cancer, justifying the review."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "past reviews in this field have noted a significant increase in their use since the early 2000s, especially in areas focused on chronic or non-communicable diseases [24, 25]. The extent to which system dynamics modeling has been applied specifically to cancer prevention and control has not been studied.",
      "reason": "Cites previous reviews and explains the need for the current review due to the specific focus on cancer."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "This is a methods review, not a review of intervention effects, as stated in the manuscript."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "This review does not focus on complex interventions or delivery contexts; it is a methods review."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 90
}

